# Test fixtures are byte-exact slices of real published electoral sources.
# Several of those sources use CRLF. With core.autocrlf=input git strips the
# CR on commit, so a fresh clone would produce a fixture that no longer matches
# the file it claims to slice. That matters here: the archive layer is defined
# by byte-exact sha256 integrity, and a line-ending-sensitive parser bug could
# never be reproduced by a silently normalised fixture.
etl/tests/fixtures/** -text

# Only the national IGN raw GeoJSON uses Git LFS; derived geometry stays outside this rule.
archive/geography/ign-argentina-country.*.geojson filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Archived source documents, when any are ever tracked, are bytes, not text.
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
